ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "6.0.2", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds a new file.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Player frame: |cffffffffMissing Mana|r in its |cffffffffVisibility|r list (Edit Mode). Tick it with |cffffffffMissing Health|r and the frame shows while either bar is below full. Thanks for the request!\n• Quality of Life › Fonts: |cffffffffZone Text|r (Default) changes the font of the zone name that appears as you enter a new area. Its size stays Blizzard's. Thanks for the request!\n• Quality of Life › Hide Clutter: |cffffffffFlag Carrier Frames|r (off) hides the two flag carrier frames under the minimap in battlegrounds. Thanks for the question!\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action bars: |cffffffffAuto Paging for Stealth|r is now |cffffffffKeep Page 1 in Stealth|r (off). The game now turns Action Bar 1 to its stealth page by itself; this option keeps your normal buttons instead. Thanks for the report!\n      - Druids keep their Cat Form page while prowling.\n      - If you had Auto Paging for Stealth off, Keep Page 1 in Stealth starts on.\n• Action bars: |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r is now off by default. Turn it on in |cffffffffBar Appearance|r.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Player cast bar: your casts never turn grey. Thanks for the report!\n      - |cffffffffRange Check|r is gone from the cast bar: with it off, every cast turned grey.\n      - Blizzard's own cast bar keeps its normal colour for your casts too.\n• Action bars: a hidden |cffffffffStance Bar|r stays hidden in combat. It came back, for example when Stealth came off cooldown, until the fight ended. Thanks for the report!\n• Action bars: with |cffffffffKeep Bar 1 in Stances|r, the spellbook's \"not on your bars\" glow matches the bar you see. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: addon buttons you keep on the minimap with the addon drawer sit above the map border. Thanks for the report!\n• Russian: the Damage Meter's |cffffffffThreat|r tab and the |cffffffffOpen Configuration|r button in Blizzard's options no longer show squares. Thanks for the report!\n• Settings: slider values such as |cffffffffDefault|r next to Bags › |cffffffffColumns|r no longer get cut off in long translations. Thanks for the report!\n• Unit frames, FlareUI Style: the last bit of shadow at the top of the portrait ring is gone.\n• Radial menu: a |cffffffffParty Spell|r slice shows the spell's name while you're alone, not your own name." },
    { version = "6.0.1", text = "|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Action bars: |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r follows Blizzard's own Cooldown Manager switch. While the Cooldown Manager is off, FlareUI leaves it alone and the option is greyed out. Thanks for the report!\n• Settings: a tab's NEW badge sits centred on the tab's top edge.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Player cast bar: your own casts keep their normal colour. Some spells turned the bar grey, whatever |cffffffffRange Check|r was set to. Thanks for the report!\n• Nameplates: with |cffffffffHide Level|r, crowd control icons sit right beside the health bar again, without a gap. Thanks for the report!\n• Unit frames, FlareUI Style: the portrait ring's rim is clean at the bottom, and nothing shows through beside the portrait.\n• Settings: long translations, such as Russian, no longer run past buttons, card titles, section headers or the page list. Text wraps, then shrinks to fit." },
    { version = "6.0", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\nFlareUI 6.0 brings a whole new settings window. We rebuilt it from the ground up, with one goal: make it as easy to use as we can. Every page now shows a live example of what it changes, drawn by the real frames, so you see the result before you leave the window. Options sit in clear sections, search takes you straight to them, and the whole window wears WoW: Forever's own bronze and stone. Tell us what still feels hard to find. Thanks to Jeor for starting this!\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffA new settings window|r: live previews, clearer pages, better search, and a look that matches the game.\n• |cffffffffCustom colours|r: pick your own colour for every unit frame and resource bar.\n• |cffffffffProfiles follow you|r: a profile now brings its frame positions to every character that uses it.\n\n|cffffd100Settings window|r\n• Every page shows a live preview of what it changes, drawn by the real frames in your current style.\n• A new |cffffffffSettings|r page holds |cffffffffSync|r, |cffffffffMove Any Window|r, |cffffffffUI Scale|r and |cffffffffLanguage|r.\n• Search shows how many options it found; press |cffffffffEnter|r to jump to the first one.\n• Module switches sit in the list on the left, so you can turn a module on or off without opening it.\n• A new look: WoW: Forever's heavy bronze frame, a stone background, stone switches and round game icons.\n• The |cffffffffsetup tour|r (/fui tour) has the same look.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Unit frames: |cffffffffColour Palette|r gets |cffffffffCustom|r. |cffffffffPick Your Colours|r opens a window with every bar colour and live samples beside them. Thanks for the request!\n      - Click a colour to change it; right-click it to go back to the palette's own. |cffffffffReset All|r clears them.\n      - Custom starts from the palette you had.\n• Resource bars: their own |cffffffffColour Palette|r (FlareUI, Blizzard or Custom), in the new |cffffffffLook|r section. Until you change it, it follows the unit frames' palette. Thanks for the request!\n• Settings: |cffffffffText Scale|r (100%), under |cffffffffUI Scale|r, makes all text larger or smaller without changing the frames. Thanks for the question!\n• Action bars: a new |cffffffffBar Appearance|r section. Thanks for the request!\n      - |cffffffffSkin Action Bars|r (on) gives every bar's buttons FlareUI's bronze frame.\n      - |cffffffffBar Scale|r (111%) sizes every button, in 0.5% steps.\n      - |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r moved here, and now frames the Essential and Utility cooldown icons too.\n• Buff Reminders: more reminders.\n      - Druids: |cffffffffThorns|r.\n      - Paladins: |cffffffffRighteous Fury|r while you're the group's tank, and an aura when none is on.\n      - Warriors: a stance when you have none.\n      - Warlocks: a |cffffffffHealthstone|r in your bags.\n      - Pets left on |cffffffffPassive|r. Click the icon to set them to Defensive.\n      - |cffffffffCamping and Rest|r (off): Forever's camp benefits and the Cozy Sleeping Bag's Well-Rested. Click to use the bag.\n      - |cffffffffGathering Tracking|r (off): Find Herbs or Find Minerals when it's off.\n• Buff Reminders: right-click an icon to |cffffffffHide Until Reload|r or |cffffffffNever Remind Me|r. |cffffffffHidden Reminders|r brings them back.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffRemind Before It Ends|r can be set apart for dungeons and raids.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffGroup Buff Filters|r hide group buffs while you're a tank, healer, damage dealer or have no role (all off).\n• Buff Reminders, in Edit Mode:\n      - |cffffffffCount Text|r (Missing / Total, Missing Only or Off), |cffffffffSpacing|r and |cffffffffOpacity|r.\n      - |cffffffffGrowth|r can start from the middle.\n      - A |cffffffffFading|r section: |cffffffffVisibility|r (Solo, In a Party, In a Raid, |cffffffffIn Combat|r), |cffffffffHide in Rested Areas|r, |cffffffffFade Speed|r and |cffffffffOpacity|r.\n• Loot Feed: |cffffffffShow Skill-Ups|r (off) adds skill gains, like \"Mining 76\", to the feed. Thanks for the request!\n• Loot Feed: font, size, outline and shadow, in a new |cffffffffQuality of Life › Fonts|r tab. Thanks for the request!\n• Tooltips › Show Tooltips: |cffffffffOn Buffs/Debuffs|r (Always) and |cffffffffOn Party/Raid Auras|r (Never). Set the second to Always or Hide in Combat to see tooltips on party and raid aura icons. Thanks for the request!\n• Swing timers: |cffffffffBar Text|r and |cffffffffTimer|r (both on), in Edit Mode's |cffffffffLook|r, hide the swing's name or the seconds left. Thanks for the request!\n• Player cast bar: |cffffffffRange Check|r (off) greys the bar while your target is out of range. It's in the cast bar's |cffffffffLook|r and in the player frame's |cffffffffCast Bar|r section. Thanks for the question!\n• Minimap: in the addon button drawer, |cffffffffShift+Right-Click|r an icon to keep that addon's button on the minimap. Do it again to put it back. Thanks for the request!\n• Loot rolls and toasts: |cffffffffScale|r in their Edit Mode dialogs.\n• Edit Mode: the Quest Tracker, Totems, Buffs/Debuffs, XP Bar and Buff Reminders get a |cffffffffFrame|r section. The tracker, the auras and the XP bar get a |cffffffffFading|r section.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Profiles: a profile's frame positions now follow it to characters on other Edit Mode layouts. Thanks for the report!\n      - Switching profiles offers the Edit Mode layout it was set up on, or explains how to copy it.\n      - |cffffffffNew|r asks whether to copy your current profile or start from defaults. |cffffffffDuplicate|r is gone.\n      - The Profiles page explains what a profile holds.\n• Shields: the part that doesn't fit after your health (all of it at full health) now shows over the health bar, from its end backwards. You see how much shield is left as you're hit. Unit frames, party and raid frames, and the Health resource bar. Thanks for the request!\n• Buff Reminders: the |cffffffffBlessing|r, |cffffffffThorns|r and |cffffffffPet Reminders|r rows are gone, to keep the page short.\n      - Pick who gets your Blessing or Thorns (|cffffffffTanks Only|r, |cffffffffOnly Me|r or |cffffffffEveryone|r) from the icon's right-click menu.\n      - Pets you turned off, and Thorns set to Off, carry over as hidden reminders.\n• Buff Reminders: |cffffffffVisibility|r, |cffffffffHide in Rested Areas|r and |cffffffffOpacity|r moved to the Edit Mode |cffffffffFading|r section.\n• Party and raid frames: Edit Mode samples show an incoming heal and a shield, as the unit frames' do. Thanks for the question!\n• Unit frames, FlareUI Style: the portrait ring keeps its full rim on the bars' side, as in Forever Style.\n• Edit Mode: every FlareUI dialog's sections start closed after a reload.\n• Edit Mode: |cffffffffRange Check|r is the first switch in |cffffffffLook|r and |cffffffffShow Level|r the first in |cffffffffFrame|r. |cffffffffSpell Pushback|r comes before |cffffffffLatency Zone|r.\n• Edit Mode: the ring's threat number sits over the middle of the ring.\n• Loot rolls: a bronze border.\n• Battleground objectives: a tidier Edit Mode sample, and the real scores sit on FlareUI's Thick plate.\n• Damage Meter: Blizzard's Edit Mode dialog for the meter no longer shows |cffffffffVisibility|r, |cffffffffTransparency|r or |cffffffffBackground|r. They did nothing with FlareUI's meter: use |cffffffffSettings › Damage Meter|r. Thanks for the report!\n• UI Scale: its tip now says |cffffffffPixel Perfect|r is about sharp borders. Text is sharp at any scale.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Unit frames: no more blocked-action errors when a druid shapeshifts in combat with the ring styles. Thanks for the report!\n• Chat: undocked windows, such as World, no longer come back lower after login, over the main chat's tabs. Thanks for the report!\n• Nameplates: with |cffffffffHide Level|r, the quest badge sits beside the health bar, not under it. Thanks for the report!\n• XP bar: the border draws over the bar, so its corners no longer show square ends. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: addon buttons on the square minimap's edge no longer sit under its border. Thanks for the report!\n• Bags: empty slots in |cffffffffIntegrated Bag Buttons|r no longer show an \"Equip Container\" tooltip." },
    { version = "5.1.2", text = "|cffffd100New|r\n• Minimap: a one-time notice when Lueur, NodeSight or Nodeworthy is on. Their node scanning makes the minimap flash, and that comes from them, not FlareUI. The Minimap settings page says so too while one is loaded. Thanks for the report!\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Loot Feed: the lowest |cffffffffMinimum Quality|r choice is now called |cffffffffAll Items|r. It already showed every item. Thanks for the feedback!\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Loot Feed: single items show again; only stacks and money did. It now also works whatever language your game is in. Thanks for the report!\n• Bags: the |cffffffffUpgrade Arrow|r no longer marks weaker gear, such as grey cloth bracers over green mail ones. Armour only gets the arrow when it loses no stat, armour included. Thanks for the report!\n• Cast bars: |cffffffffHide Spell Timer|r stays on after the first cast. Thanks for the report!\n• Minimap: no black box while gathering addons scan. Thanks to Jeor for the fix!\n• Settings: tabs no longer run past the edge of the page when they show NEW." },
    { version = "5.1.1", text = "|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating|r (not just /reload): this version adds new files.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffMoved frames come back.|r Since 5.1, a unit frame moved in Edit Mode could vanish or get stuck in the top-right corner. Fixed, and lost frames return to where you dropped them. Thanks for the reports!\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders|r, a |cffffffffLoot Feed|r and a |cffffffffMouse Ring|r, with more of what you asked for from other addons.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• |cffffffffRussian|r translation. Pick it in |cffffffffSettings › Language|r, or let FlareUI follow your game's language. Thanks to parchinskiy for the translation!\n• Buffs and debuffs: |cffffffffBuff Reminders|r (off), on its own |cffffffffBuff Reminders|r tab. Thanks for the request!\n      - An icon for each of your class's buffs missing on you or your group, or about to run out. Click it to cast the buff.\n      - Covers group buffs, self buffs, weapon imbues and poisons.\n      - Paladins: |cffffffffBlessing|r (Automatic) gives warriors, rogues and hunters Might, and everyone else Wisdom, or one blessing for everyone.\n      - |cffffffffPet Reminders|r (on): hunters call, revive or mend their pet; warlocks summon theirs.\n      - |cffffffffFood and Flask|r (off): a reminder in dungeons and raids, or always.\n      - |cffffffffWhen It Shows|r: Solo, In a Party, In a Raid, |cffffffffHide in Rested Areas|r (off) and |cffffffffOnly When You're the Only Provider|r (off).\n      - |cffffffffAlerts|r: a |cffffffffSound|r (off) and gold or orange glows (off).\n      - Edit Mode: |cffffffffOrientation|r, |cffffffffGrowth|r and |cffffffffIcon Size|r. Hidden in a fight.\n• Quality of Life: a |cffffffffBags and Looting|r tab, with the bag options, looting and the new Loot Feed.\n• Bags: |cffffffffKeyring in Backpack|r (off) and |cffffffffCrafting Bag in Backpack|r (off) add them to the bottom of the combined backpack. Thanks for the request!\n• Looting: |cffffffffLoot Feed|r (off) floats what you loot up beside you, so you don't have to read the chat. Thanks for the request!\n      - |cffffffffPosition|r: |cffffffffAt the Cursor|r (default), or |cffffffffWhere Placed|r in Edit Mode.\n      - |cffffffffMinimum Quality|r (Poor) and |cffffffffShow Money|r (on).\n• Quality of Life › Gameplay › Cursor: |cffffffffMouse Ring|r (Off) puts a bronze ring round your cursor: |cffffffffAlways|r, |cffffffffIn Combat|r or |cffffffffWhile Right-Clicking|r.\n      - |cffffffffSize|r (40) and |cffffffffThickness|r (3).\n      - |cffffffffCast Ring|r, |cffffffffGCD Ring|r and |cffffffffSwing Ring|r arcs (off).\n      - |cffffffffOut-of-Range Colour|r (off) turns it red while your target is out of reach.\n      - |cffffffffClass Colours|r and |cffffffffHide While Turning|r (off).\n• Quality of Life › Advanced: |cffffffffUI Scale|r (Blizzard's) sets the size of the whole interface as you log in. Pick |cffffffffPixel Perfect|r, a preset for 4K, 1440p or 1080p screens, or |cffffffffCustom|r (30% to 200%). Thanks for the request!\n• Quality of Life › Interface: |cffffffffWider Vendor Window|r (off) shows 20 items a page.\n• Minimap: |cffffffffOpen on Mouseover|r (off), under |cffffffffAddon Button Drawer|r, opens the drawer when you point at the day/night button. Thanks for the request!\n• Chat › Formatting, all off. Thanks for the request!\n      - |cffffffffRace Icons|r and |cffffffffClass Icons|r before player names.\n      - |cffffffffItem and Spell Icons|r inside links.\n      - |cffffffffWhisper Markers|r: a green > for whispers you get, a red < for ones you send.\n      - |cffffffffColon After Names|r: \"[Aria]: hello\".\n• Chat: with |cffffffffBetter Player Names|r on, Say lines start with a clickable |cffffffff[Say]|r label (|cffffffff[S]|r with short channel names). Click it to switch your chat back to Say. Thanks to parchinskiy for the feature!\n• Unit frames: |cffffffffRange Check|r (on), in the Look section of the target, focus, party, raid and boss frames. Off, the frame never fades for distance. Thanks for the report!\n• Resource bars: |cffffffffRange Check|r (on) for the three swing timers.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffBuy More Than One Stack|r is now |cffffffffEnhanced Vendor Purchases|r, with |cffffffffStack|r and |cffffffffMAX|r buttons, items that don't stack, and its progress above the vendor window. Your setting carries over.\n• Chat: |cffffffffShort Channel Names|r is now |cffffffffChannel Names|r: |cffffffffFull|r, |cffffffffShort|r (\"[2. Trade]\") or |cffffffffNumber|r (\"[2]\"). If you had it on, you get Number.\n• Chat: the |cffffffffFormatting|r options are in a new order.\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffConvenience|r is now at the top of the Gameplay tab.\n• Action bars: |cffffffffSkin Cooldown Manager|r moved to the bottom of |cffffffffTweaks|r. Your setting carries over.\n• Player frame: the |cffffffffMana on Shapeshift|r bar is as tall as the power bar, so its number is easier to read. Thanks for the report!\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffCompare with Shift|r is now off by default.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Unit frames: frames moved in Edit Mode no longer vanish or jump to the top-right corner. Thanks for the reports!\n• Resource bars: swing timers now turn red when your target is out of range.\n• Minimap: addon buttons on the edge of the square minimap no longer slip behind its border. Thanks for the report!\n• Settings and tour: buttons grow to fit longer translated labels, and the profile buttons move to two rows when they need the room. Thanks to parchinskiy for the fix!" },
